Now performance with numpy:

```python
import numpy as np
def minOperations(self, nums, sum):
    S = sum
    INF = 10**9
    dp = np.full(S+1, INF, dtype=np.int64)
    dp[0] = 0
    for x in nums:
        opts = {}
        k = 0
        p = x
        while p > 0:
            v = p
            j = 0
            while v <= S:
                c = k + j
                if v not in opts or c < opts[v]:
                    opts[v] = c
                v <<= 1
                j += 1
            p >>= 1
            k += 1
        nd = dp.copy()
        for v, c in opts.items():
            nd[v:] = np.minimum(nd[v:], dp[:S+1-v] + c)
        dp = nd
    return int(dp[S]) if dp[S] < INF else -1
```

Options per item ~85; numpy calls 8500; fine.

